{% comment %}
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SEATOPIA OMEGA-3 MAP — Shopify Liquid Section
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Total Omega-3 = EPA + DHA + ALA  ·  Marine Omega = EPA + DHA
  Canonical basis: mg per 100 g edible portion (values stored per 100 g)
  Display toggle: Per Seatopia Recommended Serving (default) or Per 100 g

  DATA PROVENANCE (single source of truth — do not edit values by hand)
  • EPA / DHA / ALA: seatopianutritionresolved.csv, last updated June 2, 2026.
      - Edacious = product-level mean across n third-party samples.
      - Light Labs = single-sample fallback where Edacious was 0 / <LOQ,
        or product exists only in Light Labs (Regal, Smoke in Chimneys).
  • Microplastics: microplasticsreference.csv (Light Labs / EMSL), 6-polymer
      FTIR panel, all results ND (not detected), LOD 1 microparticle.
  • Serving sizes: nutrition_products.csv "Serving Size (oz)".
  • Microplastics COA PDF links + test dates: Seatopia master sheet
      (gid=0, "Microplastics COA Link" column).

  CHANGES FROM PRIOR VERSION (2026-07-11 rebuild)
  1. Brand: Seatopia palette + type (Crimson Pro display / DM Sans body).
  2. Data: every omega value re-derived from the June 2 2026 canonical
     resolved file. Values now stored per 100 g; per-serving is derived.
  3. Data-viz best practices: title states the takeaway; source + sample
     count + basis shown on every view; removed the avg/"last test" toggle
     (a single sample was overstating some products — we now show the
     aggregated mean with n, per project data rules); EPA/DHA/ALA use
     redundant direct labels + a legend (colorblind-safe); bars sorted and
     zero-based; a Reference footer cites files + dates.
  4. Microplastics: COA PDF links + test date surfaced where published.
  5. 2026-07-11 COA link update: full set of microplastics COA links from
     the master sheet added for every tested farm; Esteros Lubimar now has
     per-product COAs (Branzino Lot BZ_EST_0001 vs Sea Bream Lot BR0001);
     Tarakan Black Tiger Shrimp COA now on file — shown as tested.
     Marshallberg Osetra: tested (Test #22503) but no published COA link
     yet (master-sheet cell blank).
  6. 2026-07-11: product/sample/COA count line moved from under the basis
     toggle into the Reference footer to reduce clutter at the top.

  SERVING-SIZE / DATA NOTES FOR REVIEW
  • Ora King serving shown as 7.5 oz (matches product page + master sheet);
    nutrition_products.csv lists an 8.5 oz pack — confirm which is canonical.
  • Caviar servings use the catalog 0.25 oz (30 g tin ÷ 4) — prior file used
    1 oz. Per-serving omega for caviar drops accordingly.
  • McFarland Springs microplastics result is the Trout Dogs variant, not the
    rainbow-trout fillet (see Claude.md mapping caveat) — flagged in tooltip.
  • Caleta Bay microplastics: COA on file (EMSL, 2025-11-06); per-polymer
    detail is on the linked COA (not in microplasticsreference.csv).
  • Black Tiger Shrimp (Tarakan): microplastics COA now on file
    (Tarakan_Monodan_ShellOff.pdf, per 2026-07-11 master sheet) — shown as
    tested; no Light Labs test # published for this one.

  INSTALL
  1. Shopify Admin → Online Store → Themes → Edit Code
  2. Create: sections/omega-map.liquid
  3. Paste this file
  4. Add via theme editor or: {% section 'omega-map' %}
